  "finding": "Across 190,961 proxy-labelled interactions from two independent ASSISTments cohorts, behavioral state prevalence is far from the uniform distribution ARIA's synthetic corpus assumes: CONFUSED accounts for 34.7% of interactions against an expected 16.7% (2.08x), while RUSHING accounts for 2.4% (0.14x). The total variation distance from uniform is 0.344 (chi-square 99,149, df 5, p < 1e-300, Cramer's V 0.3222). A synthetic corpus balanced across states is therefore a reasonable training set but not a model of classroom prevalence, and should not be cited as one."
